From: openRuyi Project Contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Resolve aliases in slice element types

Resolving an alias for the slice does not resolve the alias for its element.
Go 1.27 always represents any as an alias, so []any was not recognized as a
slice of empty interfaces. Resolve the element before inspecting it; the
existing unit and analyzer tests retain their expected diagnostics.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Upstream: https://github.com/alingse/asasalint

diff --git a/asasalint.go b/asasalint.go
--- a/asasalint.go
+++ b/asasalint.go
@@ -160,7 +160,7 @@ func isSliceAnyType(typ types.Type) (r bool) {
 	if !ok {
 		return
 	}
-	elemType, ok := sliceType.Elem().(*types.Interface)
+	elemType, ok := types.Unalias(sliceType.Elem()).(*types.Interface)
 	if !ok {
 		return
 	}
